cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these corrections, readings or glosses, please cite this repository, and credit Perseus (Tufts University) and Helma Dik / Logeion (University of Chicago) for the dictionary text they rest on."
type: dataset
title: "LSJAI: the Liddell-Scott-Jones lexicon as edited for Logeion, with corrections read by AI readers and their evidence"
authors:
  - family-names: Hartzler
    given-names: Bruce
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/bhartzler/LSJAI"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
version: "2026-10-30"
abstract: "A fork of LSJLogeion (Helma Dik, University of Chicago), the Perseus LSJ as edited for Logeion, with 1,228 corrections to the dictionary's text read by AI readers against a second digital copy and, in doubtful cases, the printed dictionary, checked by a second AI reader and applied by an AI agent, each recorded with its evidence; 41,612 readings of the entries' citations against the texts cited; and 2,481 short meanings. METHOD.md says how it was made."
keywords:
  - Greek lexicon
  - Liddell-Scott-Jones
  - LSJ
  - Logeion
  - Perseus
  - corrections
  - citations
references:
  - type: software
    title: "LSJLogeion"
    authors:
      - family-names: Dik
        given-names: Helma
    repository-code: "https://github.com/helmadik/LSJLogeion"
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
  - type: data
    title: "A Greek-English Lexicon (Liddell, Scott, Jones), the Perseus Digital Library's digitization"
    authors:
      - name: "Perseus Digital Library, Tufts University"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/PerseusDL/lexica"
